From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1q9lugp <lackowork84@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:50:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/31] v3d: 3.3 vector TMU loads need the vector's alignment

nir_opt_load_store_vectorize merged neighbouring 32-bit UBO loads into
vec2/vec3 loads at 4-byte offsets (allowed on 4.x, where a vector only
must not cross 16 bytes). On 3.3 those read wrong data: all six failing
GLES3 ubo.random.scalar_types cases (2, 3, 5, 6, 14, 23) have a vec2 or
vec3 load at offset 4, none of the 19 passing ones has a vector load
off 8/16 bytes. Only vectorize on 3.3 when the vector is aligned to 8
bytes (vec2) or 16 bytes (vec3/vec4).
---
 src/broadcom/compiler/nir_to_vir.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/broadcom/compiler/nir_to_vir.c b/src/broadcom/compiler/nir_to_vir.c
index ae53783..6a591ec 100644
--- a/src/broadcom/compiler/nir_to_vir.c
+++ b/src/broadcom/compiler/nir_to_vir.c
@@ -2054,6 +2054,8 @@ mem_vectorize_callback(unsigned align_mul, unsigned align_offset,
                        nir_intrinsic_instr *high,
                        void *data)
 {
+        struct v3d_compile *c = data;
+
         /* TMU general access only supports 32-bit vectors */
         if (bit_size > 32)
                 return false;
@@ -2073,6 +2075,16 @@ mem_vectorize_callback(unsigned align_mul, unsigned align_offset,
         if (16 - align_mul + align_offset + num_components * 4 > 16)
                 return false;
 
+        /* On 3.3 a vector access also needs the vector's own alignment
+         * (8 bytes for vec2, 16 for vec3/vec4): a vec2 or vec3 load at a
+         * 4-byte offset returned wrong data.
+         */
+        if (c->devinfo->ver < 41 && num_components > 1) {
+                unsigned vec_align = num_components == 2 ? 8 : 16;
+                if (align_mul < vec_align || align_offset % vec_align != 0)
+                        return false;
+        }
+
         return true;
 }
 
@@ -2158,6 +2170,7 @@ v3d_optimize_nir(struct v3d_compile *c, struct nir_shader *s)
                                  nir_var_mem_global,
                         .callback = mem_vectorize_callback,
                         .robust_modes = 0,
+                        .cb_data = c,
                 };
                 bool vectorize_progress = false;
 
